  "body": "## What changed\nA stepover or stepdown that's too small to ladder is now refused by name at generate. It no longer allocates until the process aborts (#691).\n\n- **The ladders:** `motion::machining2d::band` (Face, zigzag pocket and slot rows) and `cut_levels` (every depth-stepping 2D op and the 3D entry ladders) now return `Result`.\n- **The check:** before allocating, `pass_budget` refuses a step that needs more than `MAX_PASSES` (100 000) passes, or one too small to advance the coordinate (`span + step == span`). The message names the parameter: `stepover 1e-9 mm over 4.000 mm needs more than 100000 passes - raise the stepover`.\n- **Callers:** face, bore, circular, contour/chain, pocket, troch/HSM pocket, slots and 3D entry propagate the refusal with `?`.\n- **Normal steps** produce byte-identical output.\n\nThe decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/691-tiny-step.md`.\n\n## Tested\n**Pinned by:** `crates/motion/tests/tiny_step.rs`\n- `a_face_stepover_too_small_to_ladder_is_refused_by_name`: 1e-9, and 1e-300 (below float resolution).\n- `a_stepdown_too_small_to_ladder_is_refused_by_name_on_face_and_contour`: staged Face and 2D Contour at 1e-9.\n- `a_small_but_real_step_still_generates`: 0.05 mm still runs.\n\n**Gate (`scripts/gate.sh quick`), on upstream main b57f8d52+:**\n- geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion (incl. `tiny_step`) and ui suites are green.\n- The app suites and the full clippy failed to compile only on `crates/app/tests/lathe_thread_travel.rs:83` (missing `hand`). That break is already on main and is tracked as #686, not this PR.\n- So I ran these instead:\n  - app lib;\n  - app `face_holes`, `face_blend`, `mill2d_b`, `mill2d_c`, `golden_cl`, `roughing2d`, `operations`, `mcp`, `corner_blend`, `control_comp`, `level_links`, `slot_caps`, `whole_model_pocket`: all green;\n  - clippy `-D warnings` on motion (all targets) and the app lib: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **Offset-ring pockets and 3D stepovers:** these generators have their own loops and don't go through `band`/`cut_levels`. They're not reported crashing, and this PR leaves them alone.\n- **Live repro:** I didn't run the MCP repro in the GUI or the CLI live. The refusal reaches it as a normal `GenError` at generate.\n\nChangelog: A stepover or stepdown too small to ladder (over 100 000 passes) is refused by name at generate instead of aborting on a huge allocation (#691)\n\nFixes #691\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
